[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Combat/Actions/ActionDefinitionResource.cs" id="2_action"]

; A dragon's three blows, authored (2026-09-05). They were previously ONE action whose hitbox was
; swapped between the jaws, wing and tail volumes every physics frame by DragonMeleeComponent — the
; damage, timing and reach were identical whichever limb was chosen, and only the volume differed.
;
; Now each is its own action with its own volume named on it, so a wing buffet can be slower and
; wider than a bite and a tail sweep can reach further than either. DragonMeleeComponent picks WHICH
; by bearing and asks for it by id; it no longer touches the hitbox at all.
;
; ⚠️ The reaches are not decoration: they are what ActionSelection filters on. A dragon at 6 m gets
; the tail, at 3 m the bite. Widen AiMaxRange and the creature starts biting from across the room.

